    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Acute left knee pain and reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "After twisting the left knee while turning and carrying a washing basket with the knee semiflexed and weight-bearing, immediate sharp medial knee pain developed. Constant ache approximately 6/10, sharp with twisting or attempting full extension. Mobilising slowly with a hobbling gait; weight-bearing is possible for short distances, and stairs are avoided. Intermittent catching when straightening from flexion, with a feeling of being stuck, but the knee can be forced straight; no true locking. Mildly increased swelling compared with the right knee yesterday, somewhat better today. No giving way or pop. Sleep disturbed by pain when rolling in bed."
      }
    },
